  "description": "Since 1914 the Panama Canal has cut the sea voyage from New York to San Francisco from about 22,500 km to about 9,500 km. Because the canal crosses Gatun Lake, 26 m above sea level, ships are raised and lowered by locks that fill by gravity, with no pumps. Each transit of the original locks uses about 200 million liters of fresh water. Original 3D animation; map and scale are approximate.",
